WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:11.930
Luxembourg is the only country in the World
whose Prime Minister is openly gay.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:16.360
We are talking about one of the most tolerant,
open minded, societies on the planet.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:20.360
In fact, having a population of around 500,000
inhabitants, 40% of them are immigrants.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:25.900
In other words, Luxembourg is the smallest
country in European Union but the one with

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.640
the biggest share of immigrants.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:36.690
Nonetheless, what made Luxembourg famous can
be summarized in just one word: MONEY.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:41.720
Yes, my dear friends at VisualPolitik, the
Grand Duchy of Luxembourg is among the top

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.620
3 wealthiest countries on Earth.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.230
Here, the minimum wage is around 2000 euros
a month.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.559
And this is the minimum wage.

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:54.149
Because the normal wage here is over 5000
euros a month.

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:59.920
For comparison, Luxembourgish people have
a GDP per capita twice as big as that of Australians

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.750
or the Danes.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:11.330
OK, OK, but now hold on just a second because
there is a little trick in this figure!

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:16.540
You see… almost half of the workers in this
country live outside of it.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:21.240
Every day, around 160,000 commute to this
country and then, they go back to their homes

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.149
in Germany, France or Belgium.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:26.870
In other words, they create wealth in the
country but they don’t live there.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:31.430
This is why, when we divide Luxembourg’s
GDP among their population, we get such an

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:35.560
enormous number.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:45.040
But even with the statistical deviations,
no one can deny that Luxembourg is kind of

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.289
a millionaire country.

00:01:46.289 --> 00:01:51.940
And this explains why its capital, Luxembourg
city, is among the cities with the highest

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.100
quality of life.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:57.689
Many of you might think this can all be explained
because Luxembourg is a fiscal haven.

00:01:57.689 --> 00:02:02.280
But the truth is other countries like MALTA
and CIPRUS have low taxes too and they are

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.850
not even half as rich as Luxembourg.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.869
So the big question here is…

00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:10.910
What does Luxembourg have that makes them
so incredibly wealthy?

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:21.390
What did they do in this country in order
to enjoy such a great quality of life?

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.110
Today we are going to answer this question.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:31.780
But before we do, let’s take a look back
at history.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:33.550
KINGS OF STEEL

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:38.720
By the year 1815, the Grand Duchy of Luxembourg
became an “independent” country

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:43.630
And I say “independent” because none of
its neighbours really recognized this independence.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:47.610
France and Prussia, what used to be Germany
back then, fought for control of the Duchy

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:54.870
on several occasions.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:58.480
In fact, despite their government’s desire
for independence, the territory of Luxembourg

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.620
was owned by King William the 3rd of The Netherlands.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.760
During these years, Luxembourg was far from
being a wealthy country.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:08.540
Most of its citizens survived thanks to agriculture
and iron mining.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:12.250
Back then, 1 out of 5 Luxembourgish people
was emigrating to America.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:16.540
Nonetheless, living between two rival countries
like France and Prussia had its advantages

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:17.540
too.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:20.020
You see, during this time, Germany didn’t
exist as a country.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:30.260
Instead, there were a lot of republics, kingdoms
and duchies, united under a confederation.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:32.910
If you want to know what a confederation is,
do click on this video.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:36.100
The truth is… all the German states traded
among them.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:40.740
They had basically created a special free
trade zone, the so called ZOLLVEREIN.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:45.820
So… in 1942, Luxembourg became a member
of this ZOLLVEREIN.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:48.630
Since then, history would never be the same.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:53.550
As I said before, poor Luxembourg was based
on two main industries: agriculture and iron

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:54.550
mining.

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:57.200
And remember, we were in the times of the
industrial revolution.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:03.660
Steel was needed for, basically, everything,
from machines to buildings.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:07.130
And Luxembourgish citizens were sitting on
a pile of Iron.

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:08.130
But not only that!

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:17.310
We are talking about a tiny country, placed
in the intersection between Germany, France

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.310
and Belgium.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:22.500
In other words, it was the perfect point to
have a railroad so they could send the iron

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.900
to all three countries.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:28.849
Out of a sudden, Luxembourg became the zero
kilometre to all those trade routes.

00:04:28.849 --> 00:04:32.480
And also one of the biggest steel providers
on the planet.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:43.000
In fact, many of those New York skyscrapers
were built with beams from this country.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:46.040
This is why the biggest Steel companies are
Luxembourgish.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:51.199
Especially, the biggest of all of them, ARCELOR
MITTAL, which you might have seen in the financial

00:04:51.199 --> 00:04:52.199
newspapers.

00:04:52.199 --> 00:04:57.150
In other words, in just a few decades, Luxembourg
got to the same level as its neighbours.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:00.930
But still it was not the economic behemoth
it is today.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:02.660
They needed a special sauce.

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:07.310
And that special sauce was this…

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:09.590
1929

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:13.230
This is the year when Luxembourg passed the
Holding Law.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.720
But wait just a minute!

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.870
Because now you might wonder…

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:18.789
What is a Corporate holding all about?

00:05:18.789 --> 00:05:21.210
Well… let’s take COCA-COLA as an example.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.080
On one hand, COCA-COLA is a beverage brand.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.680
But on the other hand there is the COCA-COLA
company.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.939
This is a big conglomerate that includes other
companies like FANTA, SCHWEPPES or COCA-COLA,

00:05:29.939 --> 00:05:34.050
the beverage brand, itself.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:38.550
OK, so this big conglomerate is called a Holding
Corporation.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:42.210
And the companies inside of it are called
SUBSIDIARY companies.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:46.349
These subsidiaries can be in different countries
and are the guys who produce and distribute

00:05:46.349 --> 00:05:47.349
the drinks.

00:05:47.349 --> 00:05:51.319
However, the role of the Holding Company is,
mainly, to manage the property of these other

00:05:51.319 --> 00:05:52.350
subsidiary companies.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:58.689
OK… so this 1929 law offered smoking good
tax conditions to those holdings.

00:05:58.689 --> 00:06:03.909
Basically, they paid around 1% tax.

00:06:03.909 --> 00:06:07.729
These were the 30s.

00:06:07.729 --> 00:06:11.189
Back then, there weren’t as many holdings
as there are today.

00:06:11.189 --> 00:06:15.509
Just remember that those were the years when
COCA-COLA was starting to expand to other

00:06:15.509 --> 00:06:16.509
markets.

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:20.229
But they were not the giant they are today.

00:06:20.229 --> 00:06:21.229
In other words…

00:06:21.229 --> 00:06:22.229
Luxembourg was growing…

00:06:22.229 --> 00:06:25.680
but not much more than other countries.

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:31.810
LUXEMBOURG vs USA CHART 60-70s

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:36.289
Nonetheless, the 70s were the times where
American companies conquered the European

00:06:36.289 --> 00:06:40.289
and Asian markets that, finally, had more
money to spend on consumer goods.

00:06:40.289 --> 00:06:43.759
During these years, many of the big corporations
we know today were born.

00:06:43.759 --> 00:06:44.759
In other words…

00:06:44.759 --> 00:06:46.020
a lot of holdings sprang up.

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:48.400
And their profit came from all around the
planet.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.010
So where did they go to set up their headquarters?

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:56.030
Well… since they could choose, they went
to the places with the best fiscal conditions.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:59.169
And Luxembourg had everything they wanted
and more.

00:06:59.169 --> 00:07:04.270
You see, by the 60s and the 70s, the country
already had a big banking industry.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:08.099
The best lawyers, accountants and economists
were living there, ready to help those big

00:07:08.099 --> 00:07:12.199
companies in order to take the biggest advantage
of those business-friendly laws.

00:07:12.199 --> 00:07:16.729
And this is how this little country got into
their SILVER decade.

00:07:16.729 --> 00:07:22.139
LUXEMBOURG vs USA CHART 80-80s

00:07:22.139 --> 00:07:27.349
Yep, believe what you see... the economy of
Luxembourg became two times bigger in less

00:07:27.349 --> 00:07:28.630
than 6 years.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:32.529
Compared to this, China or Singapore’s growth
rate is a joke.

00:07:32.529 --> 00:07:33.550
And yes, you heard that right…

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:38.240
I said the ‘SILVER DECADE’ because all
of this growth was nothing compared with what

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:39.300
came after.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:42.569
Think about it, we are already talking about
the 2000s.

00:07:42.569 --> 00:07:45.279
The time of the online business boom.

00:07:45.279 --> 00:07:51.059
These brand new corporate juggernauts operated
all over the world, had dozens of subsidiary

00:07:51.059 --> 00:07:55.949
companies in every country and they were not
based in any specific territory because they

00:07:55.949 --> 00:08:01.360
sold everywhere.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:02.360
In other words…

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:04.360
the technological companies were made to love
Luxembourg.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:10.860
So… if you thought a country that was already
astoundingly rich, couldn’t grow more…

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:13.479
well… think twice.

00:08:13.479 --> 00:08:17.839
LUXEMBOURG vs USA CHART 2000s

00:08:17.839 --> 00:08:20.460
Amazing, isn’t it?

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:25.659
I don’t know if you noticed this but...
in just 5 years, Luxembourg’s GDP per capita

00:08:25.659 --> 00:08:31.919
went from 50,000 USD, which is already a lot,
to over 100,000 USD.

00:08:31.919 --> 00:08:35.880
When you live in a country with a GDP per
capita of over 100,000 USD…

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:37.890
well… you can fill your swimming pool with
Champaign.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:39.089
*HERE YOU CAN PUT ANY FUNNY EXAGERATION TO
EXPRESS HOW RICH YOU ARE*

00:08:39.089 --> 00:08:42.222
In fact, the AUDI a3 is the 3rd best selling
car in Luxembourg.

00:08:42.222 --> 00:08:52.680
And yes, I know what you are thinking!

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:57.510
You think that this country has made its fortune
by helping companies avoid paying their taxes,

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:58.510
right?

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:01.130
Well… the answer is a little bit more complex
than this.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:05.180
You see, the fact that a Holding corporation
is located in Luxembourg does not mean its

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:07.720
subsidiary companies don’t pay taxes elsewhere.

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:10.690
For instance, AMAZON has its headquarters
in Luxembourg.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:14.130
Nonetheless, its British subsidiary, that
is, the company that sells products and manages

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:17.690
logistics in this country, has to pay their
taxes in the UK.

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:20.330
Or… at least, this is the theory.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:23.360
In fact, the reality is way different…

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:24.630
LUXLEAKS

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:28.130
Let’s get back to the AMAZON example.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:31.970
As we said, the profits of its British subsidiary
are taxed in UK, right?

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:36.450
Well… but what happens if they have no profits
whatsoever?

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:40.850
Imagine that, right after they pay taxes,
Amazon UK gets a big loan: a big loan with

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:45.460
a really high interest rate, so high that
the company takes losses.

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:47.780
And who lends that money?

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:48.780
Exactly!

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:50.080
AMAZON HOLDINGS in Luxembourg.

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:53.730
This way, the subsidiary companies have almost
no profits.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:57.100
One way or another, they manage to send their
Money to the Luxembourgish branch.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:02.770
And, as we said before, in Luxembourg, taxes
are really low for companies.

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:07.910
Of course, all of this is perfectly legal.

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:11.880
But in 2009, during the big financial crisis,
the American government realized this huge

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:28.140
amount of money they were losing with all
of these big companies moving overseas.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:31.250
Since then, other governments have followed
Obama’s steps.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:35.040
Don’t forget Luxembourg is one of the European
Union’s founding members.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:39.690
This means the other club members were angry
and willing to lay on a lot of political pressure.

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:43.630
But the biggest crisis in this country came
in the year 2014.

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:55.150
This was the time when a group of accountants
released lots of private data from big corporations.

00:10:55.150 --> 00:11:00.830
Thanks to the so-called LUX LEAKS, we could
all see those tax evasion strategies made

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:02.090
by thousands of companies.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:06.600
Do you remember what I told you about loans
between different subsidiary companies within

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:07.600
a holding?

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.750
Well… here is another way of improving the
deal.

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:10.750
You see…

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:15.260
all these big companies hire big consulting
firms so they can help them with their accounting.

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:19.870
Consulting firms like PRICE WATERHOUSE COOPERS
with a big customer portfolio in Luxembourg.

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:24.250
They had enough power to sit down with the,
back then, Prime Minister, Jean-Claude JUNCKER

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:27.080
and arrange a special tax deal.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:32.190
“Juncker in spotlight after Luxembourg tax
revelations”

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:37.920
The leaked documents demonstrate tax arrangements
negotiated by PricewaterhouseCoopers

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:41.060
As you can imagine, the release of the LuxLeaks
is a total game-changer.

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:46.530
In fact, this year, 2017, Luxembourg has passed
a brand new fiscal reform.

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:50.480
And, probably, many of these arrangements
will have to change.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:55.190
But wait a minute because this does not mean
Luxembourg is going to stop being rich!

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:58.560
In fact, the opposite is true.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:05.350
Actually, despite these political turbulences,
the country grew at a 4.2% rate last year.

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:08.510
This is way faster than almost any other country
in Europe.

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:13.050
Having so much savings, Luxembourg has invested
in many other industries.

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:15.690
Of course, they have the steel, the banks
and…

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:19.090
THE SPACE!

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:26.580
“Luxembourg's Bet On Space Industry Shows
Early Signs Of Success”

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:27.580
You heard that right.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:31.290
In fact, Luxembourg and the United States
are the first countries to pass laws regulating

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:32.540
Space mining.

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:36.730
And this tiny country is expected to become
the Silicon Valley of the Aerospace industry.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:40.890
This explains, partly, some of the details
of this 2017 fiscal reform!

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:44.280
Of course, the Government of Luxembourg doesn’t
want to keep helping big corporations avoid

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:45.280
taxes.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:46.460
At least, this is what they say officially.

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:50.670
Instead, they have reduced taxes for smaller
companies, and are actively trying to improve

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:55.600
conditions in order to encourage more tech
startups.But… we will talk about this in

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:57.920
another video.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:02.310
Now the question for you is…

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:06.770
Do you think we will see another time of skyrocketing
growth in Luxembourg’s economy?

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:09.980
Will this country become the World’s leader
in the Aerospace industry?

